@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+---
+tier: quick
+created: 2026-09-20
+status: in-progress
+owner: node
+branch: HEAD
+touches: [src/flask/app.py, src/flask/ctx.py, tests/test_appctx.py, tests/test_reqctx.py]
+---
+
+# teardown-error-collection
+
+## Why
+Teardown failures currently stop later callbacks and can prevent the active
+context from being restored.
+
+## What
+- Collect teardown callback and signal errors while continuing request and
+  application-context cleanup in their established order.
+- Raise the collected errors only after context-local state is restored.
+- Preserve the behavior with request-context regression coverage.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] Every request and app teardown callback and signal is attempted after
+  earlier teardown failures — test: `test_teardown_continues_after_errors_and_resets_context`.
+- [x] Collected teardown errors are raised after context-local state is reset
+  — test: `test_teardown_continues_after_errors_and_resets_context`.
+- [x] Existing app-context behavior remains valid — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`.
+
+## Impact
+`AppContext.pop` is the shared request/app-context exit path used by request
+handling, CLI contexts, and test contexts. `Flask.do_teardown_request` and
+`Flask.do_teardown_appcontext` remain callable independently, preserve reverse
+registration order, and continue to send their respective signal last.
